nsider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Upbound Group, Inc., a technology and data-driven company, provides financial solutions in the United States, Puerto Rico, and Mexico. It operates through four segments: Acima, Rent-A-Center, Brigit, and Mexico. The company also provides furniture, including mattresses, tires, consumer electronics, appliances, tools, handbags, computers, and accessories. In addition, it offers merchandise on an installment sales basis; and the lease-to-own transaction to consumers who do not qualify for traditional financing, the lease-to-own transaction through staffed or unstaffed kiosks located in third-party retailer's locations, and other virtual options. Further, the company provides various financial health products and tools through mobile and web applications. It operates retail installment sales stores under the Get It Now and Home Choice names; lease-to-own and franchising location under the Rent-A-Centre and RimTyme trade names; and company-owned stores, franchise stores, and e-commerce platform through rentacenter.com, getitnowstores.com, and homechoicestores.com. The company was formerly known as Rent-A-Center, Inc. and changed its name to Upbound Group, Inc. in February 2023. Upbound Group, Inc. was incorporated in 1986 and is based in Plano, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Fahmi  Karam CPA | CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $390K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Upbound Group, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.5B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 63% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $239M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7280202403542063},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 82% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 64% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Upbound Group (UPBD) is a Top Momentum Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029517/why-upbound-group-upbd-is-a-top-momentum-stock-for-the-long-term?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3029517","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577804.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Upbound Group (UPBD) Stock Still Seems Undervalued On Its 64% Monthly Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nasdaq-upbd/upbound-group/news/upbound-group-upbd-stock-still-seems-undervalued-on-its-64-m","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479427.474,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Upbound Group (NASDAQ:UPBD) EVP Scott Young Purchases 6,015 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/upbound-grou